.TH "pocket_dump" "1" "" "" "Pocket SDR"
.SH NAME
pocket_dump \- Capture digital IF data from Pocket SDR FE or SoapySDR device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pocket_dump [\-t tsec] [\-r] [\-p bus[,port]] [\-c conf_file] [\-q] [\-v]
            [\-driver name] [\-fmt {CS8|CS16}] [\-f fs] [\-fo freq[,...]]
            [\-gain gain] [\-bw bw] [\-gpio val] [\-NO_SYNC]
            [path [path ...]]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture and dump digital IF (DIF) data from a Pocket SDR FE device or a SoapySDR\-supported device.
Pocket SDR FE capture writes one output file per RF channel unless \f[CR]\-r\f[R] is specified.
SoapySDR capture writes one complex sample stream to the first output path; with multiple RF channels the channels are written channel\-planar in blocks of a processing cycle, which
\f[CR]pocket_trk\f[R] replays as a multi\-channel input.
Capturing stops on the configured duration (\f[CR]\-t\f[R]), or by Ctrl\-C.
A \f[CR]<path>.tag\f[R] companion file is written for each output, recording the IF format, sampling rate, LO frequencies, and per\-CH sampling type / bit width so downstream tools
(e.g.\ \f[CR]pocket_trk\f[R], \f[CR]pocket_acq\f[R]) can auto\-configure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-t tsec\f[R]
Capture duration in seconds.
\f[CR]0\f[R] or omitted: capture until Ctrl\-C.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R]
Dump the raw bit\-packed device output without per\-channel separation or quantization.
With \f[CR]\-r\f[R], only the first output path is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-p bus[,port]\f[R]
USB bus and port number of the target device.
Without this option, the first device found is selected.
.TP
\f[CR]\-c conf_file\f[R]
Configure the device with a \f[CR]pocket_conf\f[R]\-format file before capture starts.
.TP
\f[CR]\-driver name\f[R]
Use a SoapySDR device instead of a Pocket SDR FE device.
Examples: \f[CR]lime\f[R], \f[CR]uhd\f[R], \f[CR]bladerf\f[R], \f[CR]rtlsdr\f[R], \f[CR]plutosdr\f[R].
Driver\-specific arguments accepted by SoapySDR can also be passed.
Multiple devices are specified as specs separated by \f[CR];\f[R], and \f[CR]nchan=<n>\f[R] in a spec selects the number of RX channels of the device (default 1), up to 8 RF channels in total.
With multiple devices the external clock and time sources are selected and the streams are started at a common time latched by a 1PPS, so a common 10 MHz and 1PPS have to be distributed to the
devices.
\- \f[CR]\-driver \(dqdriver=uhd,serial=31A1;driver=uhd,serial=31B5\(dq\f[R] \- \f[CR]\-driver \(dqdriver=uhd,serial=31A1,nchan=2\(dq\f[R]
.TP
\f[CR]\-fmt {CS8|CS16}\f[R]
SoapySDR sample format.
[\f[CR]CS8\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-f fs\f[R]
SoapySDR sampling rate in MHz.
[\f[CR]12\f[R]]
.TP
\f[CR]\-fo freq[,...]\f[R]
SoapySDR RF center frequency of each RF channel in MHz.
This option is required with \f[CR]\-driver\f[R].
A channel with an omitted or \f[CR]0\f[R] frequency uses the frequency of the first channel.
.TP
\f[CR]\-gain gain\f[R]
SoapySDR RF gain in dB.
Omitted or \f[CR]0\f[R]: use automatic gain if the driver supports it.
.TP
\f[CR]\-bw bw\f[R]
SoapySDR RF bandwidth in MHz.
Omitted or \f[CR]0\f[R]: leave driver default.
.TP
\f[CR]\-gpio val\f[R]
Output \f[CR]val\f[R] (0\-255) to the GPIO pins of the SoapySDR device (USRP: front\-panel GPIO).
The pins are set to outputs at the device open.
.TP
\f[CR]\-NO_SYNC\f[R]
With multiple SoapySDR devices, do not synchronize the device times by a 1PPS.
The devices run on their own clocks and the RF channels of different devices are NOT aligned in samples.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R]
Suppress the runtime status display.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]
Print version and exit.
.TP
\f[CR][path [path ...]]\f[R]
Output file paths.
The k\-th path is the file for CH(k); trailing paths can be omitted (those CHs are not written).
With \f[CR]\-r\f[R], only the first path is used.
\- \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R] discards the data for that CH; \f[CR]\-\f[R] writes to stdout (binary mode on Windows).
\- If all paths are omitted, the default paths are: \- \f[CR]chN_YYYYMMDD_hhmmss.bin\f[R] for each CH N (UTC start date/time).
